# Visible in the Godot 2D editor

Build visuals as scenes so they can be opened and edited in the 2D editor.

## Screens

Put panels, anchors, containers, theme overrides, and default text on the `.tscn`. Scripts wire signals, track state, and fill text that changes. `scenes/ui/game_menu.tscn` is the pattern.

## Small visual elements

A card, row, chip, badge, damage number, flash, or similar look gets its own scene, even when it is not a full screen. `scenes/ui/mech_card.tscn` is the pattern. Scripts `preload` that scene, `instantiate` it, and set the data for each copy.

## Spawned actors

A mech or prop is a scene. Spawn code only places instances.

## Existing screens

If a screen already builds its layout in code, ask before moving that whole layout into a scene. Small visual elements may be extracted into their own scenes as part of the task.

## Stay in scripts

Rules, combat math, turn flow, and AI stay in scripts and resources. Nodes display that state and emit signals for input. Do not assemble a look with `Button.new()`, `Label.new()`, `Control.new()`, or `StyleBoxFlat.new()`.
